# The home 4K split (knowledge/reference/4k-split-monitor-layout.md), read by
# tools/monitor-split. One 3840x2160 canvas: a single 4K output (one cable),
# or the two 1920x2160 picture-by-picture inputs side by side (two cables).
# An area that exactly covers an output stays that output; any other area is
# carved out of the output holding it as an xrandr virtual monitor OUTPUT~N,
# numbered per output in the order listed here.
#
#   canvas WxH
#   area NAME WxH+X+Y ROLE          offsets relative to the canvas; ROLE is a
#                                   polybar MONITOR_* role, or - for none
#   workspaces AREA N...            i3 workspaces moved there, in this order
#   focus N...                      workspaces shown last, the final one focused
canvas 3840x2160
area main 1920x2160+0+0 MAIN
area top 1920x1080+1920+0 SPLIT_TOP
area bottom 1920x1080+1920+1080 SPLIT_BOTTOM
workspaces main 1
workspaces bottom 2
workspaces top 3 5
focus 3 1
